            <ArticleTitle>Sciatica and epidural gas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epidural gas in the patient with sciatica can sometimes provide a clue that there is a surgically treatable lesion. Our patient had the sudden onset of sciatica at night, which was relieved by walking. An intraspinal synovial cyst was associated with epidural gas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
